permalink: /contact/
description: How to reach the people maintaining this letter, report a problem with the site, or correct a signature.
---

<div class="grid-container">
  <article class="usa-prose page margin-top-6 margin-bottom-6">
    <h1>Contact</h1>

    <p>
      The fastest route for anything about a signature or the site is a pull
      request or an issue on the repository, because those are public and leave a
      record others can check.
    </p>

    <h2>Correcting your signature</h2>

    <p>
      If your name is listed with the wrong organization or link, open a pull
      request against
      <a class="usa-link" href="{{ site.repoUrl }}">the repository</a> correcting
      your entry. Signatories control their own details, and no permission is
      needed to fix one.
    </p>

    <p>
      If you would rather not open a pull request, email
      <a class="usa-link" href="mailto:{{ site.contactEmail }}">{{ site.contactEmail }}</a>
      and say which entry needs changing.
    </p>

    <h2>Problems with the site</h2>

    <p>
      Broken links, layout problems, and accessibility barriers are worth
      reporting. Please include the page URL and what you expected to happen.
      The repository is at
      <a class="usa-link" href="{{ site.repoUrl }}">{{ site.repoUrl }}</a>.
    </p>

    <p>
      If you find a way to sign on someone else's behalf through this site's
      tooling, please report it privately to
      <a class="usa-link" href="mailto:{{ site.contactEmail }}">{{ site.contactEmail }}</a>
      rather than in a public issue.
    </p>

    <h2>Media and research inquiries</h2>

    <p>
      For press or research questions about the letter, contact
      <a class="usa-link" href="mailto:{{ site.contactEmail }}">{{ site.contactEmail }}</a>.
      Please note that individual signatories speak for themselves unless they
      have said otherwise, so we can only connect you with them if they have
      agreed to be contacted.
    </p>

    <h2>What we cannot do</h2>

    <p>
      We cannot remove a signature at a requester's request without their
      agreement, endorse the letter on anyone's behalf, or speak for any federal
      agency. We are private citizens and this is not a government website.
    </p>
  </article>
</div>
